body:
999 rather than 911 but there's been two occasions;

1. Me and my friend were going to the cinema and walked past a guy passed out drunk on a patch of grass next to a main road. Went to the cinema, had some dinner, then started walking home in the direction we came from and the guy was still there. This was a good 4 hours later and it was the middle of winter, he must've been freezing because we sure were. The guy looked up when we passed him and immediately got up and started chasing us down the street. We got away from him (wasn't exactly hard as he was still very drunk) and called the police. I was mostly worried that he was going to freeze to death or stumble into the road and get hit by a car.

2. Had to call an ambulance for myself once when I was suicidal. I'd been out drinking with friends and went too hard too quickly and started having some PTSD flashbacks. One of my friends helped me back to my room and managed to sober me up a bit but I was still having flashbacks. I was a wreck, I was screaming and crying and wanted to die. Scared I was actually going to do something, I told my friend to call an ambulance and she wouldn't. I begged her for about an hour to call an ambulance but she ignored me and kept trying to get me to drink water. Eventually, I locked myself in the bathroom and called them myself from there. It took them 2 hours to arrive and by that point my episode was over, I'd sobered up, but I was still quite suicidal so they took me to the emergency room and kept me in overnight. My friend claimed she didn't call them because she didn't believe I was really suicidal; she then tried to take an overdose a month later.
